WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.140
He [David Crawford, Dez Crawford’s late husband] wanted the radio station not to be the orphan, red-haired stepchild of the university.

2
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:16.520
And he struggled to get funding.

3
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:24.840
Things like chairs . . . I mean, everything from chairs to tape, to degaussers,

4
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:31.420
to a microphone that didn’t collapse every time you put it up in the air [laughs].

5
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:44.700
To finally successfully lobbying Congressman Billy Tauzin to get a power increase for the station, which we already had in hand.

6
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.360
He worked very hard for that.

7
00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:51.680
He went to Congressman Tauzin and said, you know, “Right now, we’re WPRG.”

8
00:00:51.680 --> 00:01:00.420
We used the PRG which was randomly thrown at us when WLSU . . . Somebody didn’t do the paperwork,

9
00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:07.780
and we lost WLSU to the University of Wisconsin at La Crosse.

10
00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:16.300
WLSU, Wisconsin La Crosse State University, because somebody didn’t bother to re-apply for the name.

11
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:23.420
I don’t recall what year that was, but that was a couple years before he [Dave] started.

12
00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.380
And he went to Billy Tauzin and said, “Look,

13
00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:30.780
we’re like . . . You can throw a rock from the Mississippi River from the edge of campus.

14
00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.520
The “K” and “W” border is right there.

15
00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.280
Can you petition the FCC for an exemption?”

16
00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:45.680
And Congressman Tauzin did and we got that exemption.

17
00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.420
That’s how we got KLSU back.

18
00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:54.840
And Wisconsin La Crosse State University had to settle for something else.

19
00:01:54.840 --> 00:02:04.680
And because Congressman Tauzin was so magnanimous, he spoke to the FCC in this very compelling way to make them say that,

20
00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.260
you know, “We had this first and we want it back.”

21
00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:14.500
My understanding is that that was a very low wattage station that basically broadcast to the dorms.

22
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:27.620
And we were trying to do something and expand our influence on the community and provide more coverage and to expand the School of Journalism.

23
00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.880
He made some very compelling arguments.

24
00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:37.220
Dave wrote most of the arguments that were presented to the FCC,

25
00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:45.740
and he worked with Congressman Tauzin and we got . . . Thanks to Dave, we got KLSU back.
